차근 `test-design` 스킬의 제3자 귀속 표시 (third-party attribution)

The judgment checklist in `SKILL.md` in this directory was distilled from one
MIT-licensed skill, listed below. The Korean text is newly written for non-developers
and is much shorter than the source: the five mocking rules, the "delete the code and
start over" strength, and the two rules about not asserting on source text were left
out on purpose (the skill body records what was left out and why). The "break one spot
for real and watch it go red" step, the pointers to `chageun:spec-gate` and
`chageun:debugging`, and the worked example of a converter that changed values while
three checks stayed green are chageun's own and are not from this source.

1. test-driven-development (Superpowers)
   Taken: name-the-break gate, hand-derived expectations (mirror assertion), no change
   detectors, watch-the-test-fail verification and its two failure branches, minimal
   code to pass, the mutation check list, and part of the rationalization table.
